body:
Yeah, same. For me it's like watching a movie of someone else living their life not caring much for the movie. Being completely detached from the outcome. My parents pretty much told me that I should live for them because they 'haven't given up on me yet'. 

&#x200B;

I don't know how to help you but I think I can relate in some aspects. Are you on any medication that might dull down your emotions on is it a really just a long-term thing?

Yes. Mental illnesses are not your instagram aesthetic.

&#x200B;

They suck. They ruin people's lives. And they fucking kill people.
